>>
endobj
1075 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (2.Variational Autoencoders \(VAEs\): A type of autoencoder that learns a probabilistic mapping of input data to a latent space. It generates new data by sampling from this latent space, ensuring smooth transitions between data points.   )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1076 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (zepanalytics.com)
/E (zepanalytics.com)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1077 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (12)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1078 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (3.Transformers \(e.g., GPT, BERT\): Transformer-based models are widely used for generating text. They use self-attention mechanisms to process and generate sequences of data, making them powerful for natural language processing tasks like text generation, translation, and summarization.   )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
1079 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (4. Autoregressive Models \(e.g., PixelCNN, WaveNet\): These models generate data sequentially, predicting the next element based on previously generated ones. They are commonly used in tasks like image generation \(PixelCNN\) and audio generation \(WaveNet\).   )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1080 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (5. Diffusion Models: These models reverse the process of adding noise to data. They learn to denoise data step-by-step and are often used for high-quality image generation.  )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1081 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (What are the main components of models used in Generative AI)
/E (What are the main components of models used in Generative AI)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1082 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Generative Adversarial Networks \(GANs\) consist of two neural networks: )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1083 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The generator and the discriminator, which work together in a process of adversarial training. Here's how they work:   )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
