/K [8]
>>
endobj
1087 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText ( 1. Generator: The generator creates synthetic data \(e.g., images, text, audio\) from random noise. Its goal is to produce data that is indistinguishable from real data. )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
1088 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (  )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1089 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (2. Discriminator: The discriminator evaluates whether a given data sample is real \(from the training set\) or fake \(generated by the generator\). It outputs a probability score indicating the likelihood of the data being real.  )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1090 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText ( )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1091 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (3. Adversarial Training: The generator and discriminator are trained together in a competitive process:   )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1092 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (oThe generator tries to create data that fools the discriminator into thinking it's real. )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1093 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (oThe discriminator tries to accurately distinguish between real and fake data. )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
