>>
endobj
1121 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (2.Data Reconstruction for Creative Generation: )
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1122 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The encoder-decoder structure allows autoencoders to take raw input, transform it to a latent representation, and then reconstruct it back to the original form. This ability is useful in tasks like image and video generation, where the model must understand the structure and texture to create something visually coherent.  )
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1123 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (2.Anomaly Detection and Data Enhancement:)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1124 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Autoencoders can highlight deviations by attempting to reconstruct data and comparing the output with the input. This is valuable in GenAI applications, such as enhancing image quality by detecting and filling in missing details or creating more realistic, high-quality variations. )
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
