<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (1. Mean Squared Error \(MSE\) / L2 Loss )
/Pg 98 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1647 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2828 0 R
/ActualText (Description: MSE calculates the average squared difference between each pixel in the generated and target images. )
/Pg 98 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1648 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2829 0 R
/ActualText (Contribution: It ensures pixel-wise accuracy, penalizing large differences in intensity between corresponding pixels. MSE is simple and computationally efficient but may produce overly smooth images as it lacks perceptual awareness. )
/Pg 98 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1649 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (2. Mean Absolute Error \(MAE\) / L1 Loss)
/Pg 98 0 R
/K [5]
>>
